  <info>
  <link type="guide" xref="inventory"/>
  <link type="seealso" xref="locations"/>
  <desc>Move stock from one location to another.</desc>
    <credit type="author">
      <name>Reuben Rissler</name>
      <email>pygtk.posting@gmail.com</email>
    </credit>
  </info>

  <title>Transfer inventory</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Inventory</gui><gui>Transfer</gui></guiseq> moves products
  between <link xref="locations"/>.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Choose where to <gui>Move from</gui> and <gui>Move
    to</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Choose a product; how many are on hand at the source is shown.
    Click <gui>Add</gui>. Adding a product already listed adds to its
    line.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click a line's <gui>Quantity</gui> to change how many move; a sum
    such as <input>2x12</input> works too (see
    <link xref="qty_arithmetic"/>). Right
    click a line to remove it or open its <gui>Product hub</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Type <gui>Notes</gui> on why the stock is moving, and click
    <gui>Transfer</gui>.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p><gui>Locations</gui> opens <link xref="locations"/> to add one.</p>

</page>
